# Optional development configuration for Auto-Pigeon Companion.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the directory you start `companion` from (for
# example this checkout, with `go run ./cmd/companion`), or point
# AUCOM_ENV_FILE at a copy anywhere. Nothing needs it: a released Companion on
# a clean machine reads no .env and works signed out; the backend address can
# also be set in the GUI (Settings) or in config.json.
#
# Read by: cmd/companion/main.go -> internal/config/envfile.go (LoadDevEnvFile).
# Only the keys listed below are honoured; any other key is reported and
# ignored. A variable already set in the real environment wins.

# Where auto-pigeon-backend (AUB) lives, written as scheme://host:port.
# A normal local stack started by launch-aup.sh serves AUB on host port 9190.
# [PRODUCT_OPTIONAL] Read by: internal/config/config.go, internal/web/settings.go
AUCOM_AUB_BASE_URL=

# Where incident reports go: the stack's GlitchTip DSN for the AUCOM project,
# written as scheme://<public key>@host:port/<project id>. Unset means nothing
# is sent anywhere — the ordinary case on a person's machine. The value carries
# an ingestion key: keep it out of anything tracked.
# [PRODUCT_OPTIONAL] Read by: internal/incident/config.go (via internal/cli)
AUCOM_INCIDENT_DSN=

# Which deployment incidents are filed under: development, production or test.
# Unset means production for a stamped `1.<n>` release, development otherwise.
# [PRODUCT_OPTIONAL] Read by: internal/incident/config.go (via internal/cli)
AUCOM_INCIDENT_ENVIRONMENT=

# AUCOM_E2E_FAULTS is deliberately NOT honoured from this file: `companion dev
# fault` is unlocked only by the real environment (see README).
